WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:04.320
Will the Yellowstone Dutton ranch finally&nbsp;
fall? Will the new sheriff make it his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:08.655
business to shut down the Duttons? These&nbsp;
questions and more from Yellowstone Season 4.

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:13.360
As the 4th season gets underway, we&nbsp;
learn that Kayce survived the attack&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:17.040
in the previous season's finale. There&nbsp;
are no magic solutions to this puzzle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:21.600
though — just Kayce's dogged determination&nbsp;
and sharp-shooting skills, which helped him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:25.600
stay alive and kill the men who came after&nbsp;
him. But in the aftermath of the attack,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:30.480
things change for Kayce and his family: Monica&nbsp;
and Tate were also targets of assassination,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:35.680
and though the pair survived thanks to Tate's&nbsp;
handling of a shotgun, they were left traumatized.

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:40.160
Looking out for the emotional well-being of&nbsp;
his family first, Kayce decides to relocate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:45.040
taking his wife and son off the Yellowstone-Dutton&nbsp;
Ranch and buying a house in Pryor, Montana.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:49.520
It seems to do wonders for young Tate and Monica,&nbsp;
too, and it's not long before she tells Kayce&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:54.080
that they are expecting another child. After&nbsp;
yet another mysterious wolf sighting, though,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:58.240
Kayce seeks the help of his friends on the&nbsp;
reservation, who convince him to undertake&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:03.440
a vision quest for answers. There, he encounters&nbsp;
images of his dead brother Lee, flashbacks of his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:07.920
time in the war, and the wolf — his spirit guide&nbsp;
— in the form of a young Native American woman.

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:12.000
With what we've seen Kayce and his family go&nbsp;
through this season and the comfort he's seemingly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:16.880
found off the ranch, we wonder if he'll keep his&nbsp;
promise to his father and return to Yellowstone.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:21.200
Is this Sheridan's way of writing Kayce out of&nbsp;
the series, or just a new story arc for him?

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:26.000
It was way back in Season 2 that Jamie's&nbsp;
ex-girlfriend Christina dropped a major&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:30.400
bombshell on him: she is pregnant with his&nbsp;
child. Jamie begged her to allow him to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:33.920
a part of the baby's life, but she announced&nbsp;
that she couldn't be with him if he was still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:38.560
working with the Duttons. Before leaving him&nbsp;
again, Christina gave Jamie a fateful choice:

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:46.080
"Serve your father's family or serve your&nbsp;
own. Like it or not, that choice is coming."

00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:51.040
It wouldn't be an immediate decision for him,&nbsp;
as Jamie does return to serve his father as a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:55.360
weapon of the ranch against his enemies. But then&nbsp;
he discovers he is not really a Dutton at all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.360 --> 00:01:59.600
having been adopted as a baby. And it's when&nbsp;
he reconnects with his birth father Garrett&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:04.000
Randall in Season 4 that Christina&nbsp;
resurfaces — with their baby in tow.

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:07.680
But after Season 4's conclusion, there&nbsp;
is still no indication that anyone else&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:10.560
in the Dutton family knows of&nbsp;
the existence of Jamie's child,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:15.360
and it's anyone's guess how they'll react when&nbsp;
they find out. Could Beth be looking for blood,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:19.120
vengefully resentful that she can't have&nbsp;
children of her own? Could John see this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:23.040
child as a possible heir to the Yellowstone,&nbsp;
as he has made it clear he still views Jamie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:26.400
as his son? We'll have to wait and see.

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:30.480
Speaking of Jamie, one major plotline that&nbsp;
is still left hanging at the end of Season&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:35.040
4 is the fate of the governor's race. The&nbsp;
adopted Dutton split away from his family&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:39.280
to pursue the office against the wishes&nbsp;
of his father and in defiance of John&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:43.280
entering his own name in the race. A&nbsp;
potential political rivalry between&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:46.720
father and son figures could be a&nbsp;
fascinating story for "Yellowstone,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:51.840
but Jamie still hasn't officially filed his own&nbsp;
candidacy, leaving the plot up in the air for now.

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:56.560
There were a few wrinkles before the 4th season&nbsp;
finale, namely the existence of Jamie's birth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.560 --> 00:03:00.960
father, Garrett Randall. With the family now&nbsp;
aware of the role Jamie's birth father played&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:05.600
in the attempt on their lives, there's a whole&nbsp;
new can of worms opened, even if Garrett himself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:10.320
doesn't survive the fourth season. But Jamie&nbsp;
insists he "had a plan" for how to deal with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:14.720
John's knowledge of his father, so we're curious&nbsp;
what that could mean. As it stands, the race to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:19.120
be Montana's next governor is just heating up&nbsp;
and could be the main story of the 5th season.

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:24.640
In the season opener, Beth meets Carter while&nbsp;
outside the hospital that her father is recovering&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:29.360
in, and the pair bond over their mutual family&nbsp;
problems. Carter's father is dying, and when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:34.160
he needs someone by his side to say goodbye, Beth&nbsp;
uncharacteristically offers to be support for him.

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:36.000
"Are you a friend of the family?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:42.000
I guess I am now."

00:03:43.520 --> 00:03:47.520
After a little tough love from Beth and Rip,&nbsp;
Carter winds up working at Yellowstone as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:52.240
a ranch hand and living with Beth and Rip in a&nbsp;
quasi-family unit. Since we learned in Season 3&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.240 --> 00:03:56.480
that Beth is unable to be a mother, we've pondered&nbsp;
what that might mean for her future on the ranch,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.480 --> 00:04:00.880
unable to be a part of her family's continuing&nbsp;
legacy. But since the introduction of the young&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:05.040
Carter, it has increasingly felt like she&nbsp;
might just have a crack at parenthood yet.

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:08.640
From Carter's introduction, it seemed&nbsp;
that he might be the next Rip Wheeler:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:12.800
a troubled, angry orphaned boy brought to the&nbsp;
ranch through a compassionate Dutton and raised&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:17.280
to be a cowboy. But in the finale, Beth makes&nbsp;
it clear she wants no part of being a mother,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:21.280
though it's hard to deny that's exactly&nbsp;
what's happening. Still, the question remains:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:26.000
What will Carter become? Will he be the next&nbsp;
surrogate Dutton like Rip, a future wrangler&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:30.480
and Yellowstone enforcer? Or with Kayce and his&nbsp;
family off the ranch — perhaps for good — could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.480 --> 00:04:34.560
Carter stand to become the next generation of&nbsp;
the Dutton family with Tate out of the picture?

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:38.480
We've seen John getting closer to Carter&nbsp;
in the same way he was bonding with Tate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.480 --> 00:04:41.840
earlier in the series, so there's no&nbsp;
telling which way this one could go.

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:44.240
For four long years on "Yellowstone,"

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:47.840
we've watched Beth Dutton's hatred&nbsp;
for her brother Jamie percolate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:50.800
a few times boiling over into overt aggression.

00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:54.320
In the 4th season's final episode, the&nbsp;
feud between the siblings reached what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.320 --> 00:04:58.560
may be its climax, with Beth discovering that&nbsp;
it was Jamie's birth father, Garrett Randall,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:03.440
who ordered the assassination attempts on the&nbsp;
Duttons. Beth gives Jamie two choices — neither&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:07.520
of which are good — before Jamie chooses&nbsp;
a third option. At the end of the episode,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.520 --> 00:05:11.920
we see Jamie murder Randall, openly weeping&nbsp;
for what he had to do to save his future.

00:05:11.920 --> 00:05:13.600
Just when he thought he was in the clear,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.600 --> 00:05:16.960
Beth appears while Jamie dumps&nbsp;
the body into the canyon.

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:19.120
"You should have picked options one or two.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:24.080
Three's gonna be worse,&nbsp;
but you're f—ing mine now."

00:05:25.520 --> 00:05:29.920
But does this threat really carry the weight&nbsp;
she seems to think it does? Her own husband, Rip&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.920 --> 00:05:34.160
Wheeler, has buried more than one murder at the&nbsp;
bottom of the same cliff, and revealing Jamie's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:39.120
involvement with Randall could threaten to expose&nbsp;
more than one family secret, including Rip's part&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.120 --> 00:05:44.000
in the cover-up of a reporter Jamie killed. Could&nbsp;
this threat come back to haunt her next season?

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:48.880
And moreover, will the death of Garrett Randall&nbsp;
have greater consequences that we don't yet see?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:53.040
There are still many questions surrounding Randall&nbsp;
that need answering, including what he's been up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:58.800
to behind Jamie's back. He seemed to be expecting&nbsp;
his death just before it came, so it may also be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.800 --> 00:06:03.680
possible he had a posthumous backup plan ready,&nbsp;
having promised to go after the Duttons again.

00:06:04.720 --> 00:06:06.880
A divisive new foil for the Dutton family,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:10.640
Summer Higgins is an environmental&nbsp;
activist added to the cast this season.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:15.920
Summer comes to town under the auspices of ending&nbsp;
animal cruelty and saving Montana's rich untamed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:15.920 --> 00:06:20.080
lands from the change that industrialists&nbsp;
are attempting to bring to the region.

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:24.960
Along the way, she becomes a pawn of Beth Dutton's&nbsp;
desire to sabotage Market Equities' land deal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.960 --> 00:06:28.960
and winds up facing life in prison&nbsp;
because of Beth's vicious machinations.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.960 --> 00:06:31.040
Thankfully, John feels it isn't right for Beth to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.040 --> 00:06:34.720
do what she did and attempts to sway&nbsp;
the judge to let Summer off the hook.

00:06:34.720 --> 00:06:35.760
"It's the right thing to do."

00:06:37.280 --> 00:06:40.160
"Right barely factors into it anymore, John."

00:06:40.880 --> 00:06:44.400
It's touch and go, but in the end,&nbsp;
Summer gets a much-reduced sentence,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:48.000
and it's said that she'll likely be freed&nbsp;
from her jail cell within a year. While&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:51.760
this may seem like the end of her story on&nbsp;
"Yellowstone," we can't help but wonder if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:56.080
there's more of a role for her to play. She's&nbsp;
still a potentially powerful ally as leader of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.080 --> 00:07:00.000
an environmentalist movement, and she and&nbsp;
John seem to share some of the same goals.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:04.160
If she's only expected to do eight months behind&nbsp;
bars, we may not have seen the last of her.

00:07:05.040 --> 00:07:08.880
At the beginning of the season, Jimmy finds&nbsp;
himself seriously injured, not by the attack&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.880 --> 00:07:14.000
on the ranch, but by a misguided attempt to rodeo&nbsp;
again, breaking his promise to John Dutton. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:17.920
he's still a member of the family, and John&nbsp;
isn't ready to give up on Jimmy altogether, so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.920 --> 00:07:24.000
he orders the young wanna-be cowboy off to Texas&nbsp;
to a notorious ranch called the "6666" — a place&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:29.680
that works their men harder than any other. If the&nbsp;
6666 can't turn Jimmy into a cowboy, nobody can.

00:07:29.680 --> 00:07:34.640
Jimmy does indeed learn to cowboy and even meets&nbsp;
Emily, who becomes his fiancée in a rapid-fire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.640 --> 00:07:39.520
romance. When Jimmy returns to Yellowstone, he&nbsp;
promises to stay until his debt to the ranch&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.520 --> 00:07:43.920
is repaid, but John graciously lets him leave&nbsp;
with Emily and start a new life at the 6666.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.720 --> 00:07:48.720
What's next for him? We likely won't get answers&nbsp;
in the next season of "Yellowstone" and will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.720 --> 00:07:53.434
instead see Jimmy's story continue&nbsp;
in the new spin-off series, "6666."

00:07:53.520 --> 00:07:58.960
In one of the season's many shocking moments, John&nbsp;
and Rip meet Sheriff Haskell at a roadside diner,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.960 --> 00:08:03.680
only to discover the restaurant is in the&nbsp;
middle of being held up by a group of lowlifes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.680 --> 00:08:08.480
Rip and John are able to turn the tables, but&nbsp;
not before the thugs fatally wound Haskell.

00:08:08.480 --> 00:08:13.360
In the penultimate episode of the season, we meet&nbsp;
Haskell's replacement, Commander Ramsey. John&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.360 --> 00:08:18.080
is clearly rattled when Ramsey is announced as&nbsp;
Haskell's interim replacement, and it’s suggested&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:23.360
that John is unsure if Ramsey can be trusted. Not&nbsp;
because he's corrupt, but because he might not be.

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:27.120
"Things will be different with me in charge."

00:08:27.120 --> 00:08:27.920
"New rules, huh?"

00:08:29.040 --> 00:08:32.000
"Still the old rules, but&nbsp;
now they'll be enforced."

00:08:33.040 --> 00:08:36.080
We only get a brief look at&nbsp;
Ramsey in his new role as sheriff,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.080 --> 00:08:39.040
but he's already made it clear he's&nbsp;
going to do things differently.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.040 --> 00:08:43.200
Ramsey seems acutely aware of Haskell's&nbsp;
corruption, setting him up to be a major&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.200 --> 00:08:48.080
thorn in the Duttons' side as the series moves&nbsp;
into its 5th season. But the question remains:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.080 --> 00:08:52.800
Will Sheriff Ramsey be a momentary roadblock,&nbsp;
or will he stick around to cause trouble?

00:08:53.600 --> 00:08:57.680
We're not suggesting for a moment that&nbsp;
Season 5 of "Yellowstone" will be the last,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.680 --> 00:09:02.640
but we could be entering a new stage of the series&nbsp;
and wonder if we might be seeing the last days of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:02.640 --> 00:09:07.360
the Yellowstone-Dutton Ranch. Surrounded by&nbsp;
enemies on all sides, there seems to be no&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.360 --> 00:09:12.000
way out for John and his family, who have all&nbsp;
but acknowledged their days could be numbered.

00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:16.640
With one of the country's biggest firms at their&nbsp;
back in Market Equities — whose principal owner&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.640 --> 00:09:21.680
now has a personal reason to go after their land&nbsp;
after Beth crossed her — and allies dropping left&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.680 --> 00:09:25.840
and right, it feels like the noose is finally&nbsp;
closing around the Duttons. Could the series'&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.840 --> 00:09:30.560
fifth year see them lose their ranch and fight&nbsp;
to get it back? It might seem like a far-fetched&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:30.560 --> 00:09:34.960
notion for a series that's built around a family&nbsp;
willing to die before they lose their land,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.960 --> 00:09:40.160
but where "Yellowstone" is concerned, there seem&nbsp;
to be no limits to the stories that lay ahead.

